  "claim_boundary": "This exact LOCAL-ALGEBRAIC/LORENTZIAN-CAUSAL spectral engine constructs the Berger-S3 de Rham matrices d_p and Hodge Laplacians Delta_p=d^dagger d+d d^dagger in any requested finite SU(2) Peter-Weyl block. It uses the certified squashing c=3 sqrt(10)/20, exact skew-Hermitian spin generators, and the orthonormal coframe equations dtheta1=-c^-1 theta2 theta3, dtheta2=c^-1 theta1 theta3, dtheta3=-c theta1 theta2. Blocks two_j=0..4 have zero d^2 defects, Hermitian Laplacians, Hodge-dual spectra, and the two_j=1 scalar eigenvalue 29/18 matching the global-rod certificate. This is an exact finite-block engine, not a validated expansion of the compact detector bumps: harmonic coefficients, quadrature bounds, spectral-tail bounds, Green images, and the absolute-g3 recoil coefficient remain open. It does not make a finite-parameter interacting or quantum claim.",
